2026-11-06T03:17:43.8980645Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-06T03:17:43.8988931Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-06T03:17:43.8989375Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-06T03:17:43.8989686Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-06T03:17:43.8989805Z 
2026-11-06T03:17:43.8989912Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-06T03:17:43.8990045Z 
2026-11-06T03:17:43.8990167Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-06T03:17:43.8990406Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-06T03:17:43.8990570Z 
2026-11-06T03:17:43.8990669Z If you would like to
2026-11-06T03:17:43.8990936Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-06T03:17:43.8991120Z 
2026-11-06T03:17:43.8991296Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-06T03:17:43.8991614Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-11-06T03:17:43.8991703Z 
